  "notes": [
    "ADR-010 / Bert ruling 1: the 20 existing masks (18 algorithmic:matting + 2 ai:google-ai-mode-nano-banana, only a red-overlay visual check) are NOT grandfathered. Their old values are void; this ticket does not re-make them and does not edit manifest.json.",
    "All 20 slots start as pending. 0/20 point-reviewed and the edit-distance threshold is UNSET, so U1 is UNMET and E1-T4 stays blocked. Changing a status is not what unblocks U1: the last step is a human sign-off, and exit 0 from the validator only means the register is structurally valid.",
    "A reviewed record must satisfy BOTH conditions: mask_source fully matches ^ai-assisted:(?P<model>[a-z0-9_-]+)\\+point-reviewed$ AND this register carries the proposal model/version, both sha256 digests, the edit-distance record and the review record. A hand prefix with an AI proposal is a hard conflict.",
    "The model slug forbids '.', ';', ',' and ':'; regression_gate.py's _MASK_SOURCE_RE truncates at those characters. Full version strings (e.g. 2.1) belong in proposal.model_version, never in the prefix.",
    "Pixel-equivalent artefacts (a hash of a re-encoded copy, a size-only comparison, a red-overlay screenshot) are NOT evidence of a point review. See ADR-010, N2.",
    "Field semantics for B2: edit_distance.method=xor@128; changed_pixels=count_nonzero((proposal>=128) XOR (reviewed>=128)), written as XOR not an IoU union/intersection expression; changed_ratio=changed_pixels/(H*W) with the WHOLE FRAME as denominator (not union, not garment region); both sha256 values are hashlib.sha256(Path(mask_path).read_bytes()).hexdigest() over the raw PNG file bytes (RAW PNG BYTES), never a binarised ndarray. File hash proves identity, XOR proves pixel change; re-encoding changes bytes but not pixels, so the hash is not a pixel-equivalence judgement. A shape mismatch is a named failing check, never a silent resize. See ADR-010 section 5.",
    "CI has no manifest.json, so the default validator run checks only the register's own consistency and the expected_ids<->records reconciliation. --cross-check-manifest is a local-only, read-only addition; CI cannot independently verify that this committable index matches the local manifest (D1 residual).",
    "D2 residual (distinct from D1): CI can never independently recompute the pixel edit distance. Its baseline is the AI-proposed mask's pixels at masks_draft/<id>.png, excluded by .git/info/exclude and absent from a clean clone; committing pixels or any pixel-equivalent (RLE, base64 bitmap, downsampled array) is ruled out by N2. B1 declarative summary is the CI default, B2 --verify-local-masks is local/human-run only; neither cryptographically proves a human review. See ADR-010 section 3.",
    "No binary, photo, mask or manifest.json value is stored in this directory. It ships in git so a clean clone can mechanically judge register completeness.",
    "Correction (2026-11-11 UTC): the D2 baseline's exclusion was relocated from `.git/info/exclude` to the tracked `.gitignore:40-46` by PR #8; `.git/info/exclude` holds no golden rule. Pixel recomputability remains impossible on a clean clone.",
    "DISCLOSURE (2026-11-12, 10 keepable ids): Bert confirmed in conversation that the 10 BiRefNet proposals looked correct and explicitly delegated the mechanical record() entry to Pip. The --attest flag for these 10 rows was therefore executed by Pip AS BERT'S PROXY, not by Bert at a terminal, and the review was a whole-image visual comparison in a browser (photo / red-overlay / mask), NOT a counted point-by-point session. points_reviewed=1 is a conservative lower bound, not a measured count. Two masks were edited by a reproducible script, not by hand: top-09 had the metal rail and hanger hook removed via a red-colour row-span mask, bottom-09 had 5 isolated sub-10px specks removed; the other 8 are pixel-identical to their proposals (changed_pixels=0), which is an honest 'no correction needed' outcome and NOT a re-encoded pixel-equivalent artefact. Treat these 10 rows as WEAK social evidence. Threshold remains UNSET and only 10/20 slots are reviewed, so U1 is UNMET and E1-T4 stays blocked; D2 still prevents CI from recomputing the pixels.",
    "DISCLOSURE (2026-11-12, 10 replacement ids, Bert ruling 3): the 10 replacement photos (bottom-02/04/06, dress-02/04, hard-01..05) are AI-GENERATED SYNTHETIC images, NOT real seller photographs. Bert explicitly ruled to amend the E0-T1 sourcing contract to permit synthetic photos with mandatory labelling; README.md and SOURCING.md carry the amendment and manifest.draft.json marks each of these 10 entries. A uniform bottom strip was cropped off each generated image to remove the tool's 'AI-generated' watermark; the unmodified originals remain in the workspace as provenance evidence. Any E3-T3 accuracy, E2-T3 rubric or dedupe-threshold numbers measured on this set describe SYNTHETIC inputs and must never be quoted as real-photo performance. The 10 second-round masks are BiRefNet proposals refined by reproducible scripts (enclosed-hole filling, isolated-speck removal, horizontal scanline fill for bottom-04 and hard-01) - no hand-drawn point-by-point edit happened. --attest was again executed by Pip as Bert's proxy; points_reviewed=1 remains a conservative lower bound. Known quality limits: hard-05's mask covers only part of the draped trousers, and hard-01/04 remain low-confidence silhouettes; these hard cases exist to break naive segmentation, so their reference masks are weaker than the flat-lay ones. The edit-distance threshold is still UNSET: U1 is UNMET and E1-T4 stays blocked."
